# draft
// DRAFT: placeholder writing to be rewritten (docs/story-drafts.md).
The gate of the slain is a long table under a grey sky, and the dead are already queuing.
A tall woman in mail sets a stamp down in front of you. # speaker: skogul
"Skögul. I'm to train you. Don't touch the axe on the left; it isn't mine." # speaker: skogul
"The rule is simple. Weapon in hand when they fell: Valhalla. Anything else: Hel. Odin can count, and so can his quartermaster." # speaker: skogul
* ["What if they lie?"]
  "They will. The dead talk; bodies don't. Look at the hands before you listen to the mouth." # speaker: skogul
  "When a story and a body disagree, compare them. That's what the brass pin is for." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: flag asked_about_lies
* ["What if I'm wrong?"]
  "Then a braggart drinks with heroes, an honest farmer goes to Hel, and the quartermaster docks your wage." # speaker: skogul
  "Two mistakes a day are forgiven. After that, you pay." # speaker: skogul
* [Pick up the stamp.]
  She almost smiles. "Good. Odin likes the ones who don't ask." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: standing odin +1
- The first of the dead shuffles forward.
-> END
